# Laryngeal Cancer Survival Analysis

## Overview

This project analyzes the survival of laryngeal cancer patients using statistical methods in R. The analysis focuses on examining survival probabilities across disease stages and evaluating the relationship between disease stage and the risk of an event.

The project applies Kaplan–Meier estimation, the log-rank test, and Cox proportional hazards regression to explore differences in survival outcomes between patient groups.

## Objectives

- Estimate survival probabilities using the Kaplan–Meier method.
- Compare survival distributions across disease stages using the log-rank test.
- Evaluate the association between disease stage and event hazard using Cox proportional hazards regression.
- Interpret statistical results to understand differences in survival outcomes.

## Dataset

This project uses the `larynx` dataset from the `KMsurv` R package.

| Variable | Description |
|---|---|
| `time` | Observed follow-up or survival time |
| `delta` | Event indicator; 1 indicates an event and 0 indicates censoring |
| `stage` | Disease stage |

## Tools and Technologies

- R
