## How to Run

1. Install R and RStudio.
2. Install the required packages:

   ```r
   install.packages("survival")
   install.packages("KMsurv")
   ```

3. Load the packages and dataset:

   ```r
   library(survival)
   library(KMsurv)

   data(larynx)
   ```

4. Perform Kaplan–Meier estimation:

   ```r
   fit.larynx <- survfit(
     Surv(time, delta) ~ stage,
     data = larynx,
     conf.type = "log-log"
   )

   summary(fit.larynx)
   plot(
     fit.larynx,
     xlab = "Time",
     ylab = "Survival Probability"
   )
   ```

5. Perform the log-rank test:

   ```r
   survdiff(Surv(time, delta) ~ stage, data = larynx)
   ```

6. Fit the Cox regression model:

   ```r
   reg.larynx <- coxph(
     Surv(time, delta) ~ factor(stage),
     data = larynx
   )

   summary(reg.larynx)
   ```

