## Limitations

- The analysis uses a single dataset.
- Results depend on the available observations and follow-up information.
- The proportional hazards assumption should be checked before drawing conclusions from the Cox model.
- Statistical associations do not establish causation.

## Conclusion

This project demonstrates the application of survival analysis techniques in R to examine survival patterns among laryngeal cancer patients. The results indicate significant differences in survival distributions across disease stages, with stage 4 showing a substantially higher estimated event hazard than stage 1.

